 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265338 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186263233 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265338 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186263826 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265338 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186264108 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265338 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186264653 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265338 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186265035 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265338 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265338 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265338 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186265035 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265338 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "33500533-1ff2-52fe-b070-b355792f8c8d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265499 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186263908 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265499 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186264012 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265499 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186264627 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265499 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186265041 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265499 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186265164 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265499 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265499 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265499 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186265041 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265499 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "8efde9f4-a558-594d-aa01-2870e1f40df1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266124 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186265499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266124 #edb/ref 1069 "q-131959" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266124 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266124 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4t⟩$ for $0\\le t<2\\pi ,$ use the cross product curvature formula to compute the curvature at the point $P(0,-3,4\\pi ).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266124 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1522196c-85d3-5761-a4c8-6c5974238241" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266124 #edb/ref 1074 "The curvature $κ(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to the point $P(0,-3,4\\pi )$ on the given curve. We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨0,-3,4\\pi ⟩ \\\\ ⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4t⟩ & =⟨0,-3,4\\pi ⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the respective components gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=0 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=-3 \\\\ 4t=4\\pi .\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equality, $t=\\pi .$ This value also satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, $P(0,-3,4\\pi )$ is at the tip of $r(\\pi ).$ \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$, ${r}^{′}(\\pi ),$  and $‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,4⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(\\pi ) & =⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,0,4⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖ & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{0}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${r}^{″}(t)$ and ${r}^{″}(\\pi ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(\\pi ) & =⟨-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,3,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross-product and its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\pi )\\times {r}^{″}(\\pi ) & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-12i-9k \\\\  & =3(-4i-3k) \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )\\times {r}^{″}(\\pi )‖ & =3\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{16+9} \\\\  & =3(5) \\\\  & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature at $t=\\pi $ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(\\pi ) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )\\times {r}^{″}(\\pi )‖}{‖{r}^{′}(\\pi ){‖}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{{5}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266128 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186265338 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266128 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132067" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266128 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266128 #edb/ref 1071 "Using the cross product curvature formula, find the curvature of $r(t)=⟨t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$ as a function of $t.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266128 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7eb005e4-b7c8-57e9-a9a3-c7cb18e5c9e7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266128 #edb/ref 1074 "The curvature $κ$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}+{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{t}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{t}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)+({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the second derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross product by considering ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${r}^{″}(t)$ as $3$-dimensional vectors with zero $z$-components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,0⟩\\times ⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & \\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & 0 \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & \\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k \\\\  & =[(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)]k \\\\  & =[2{cos}^{2}⁡t-3t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{t}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡t+2{sin}^{2}⁡t+3t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{t}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡t]k \\\\  & =(2({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)+{t}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t))k \\\\  & =({t}^{2}+2)k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the magnitude of the cross product is\n\n$$\n‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖={t}^{2}+2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}+2}{{(\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1})}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}+2}{({t}^{2}+1)^{3/2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315399 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315399 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315399 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "31064109-55cc-5be1-9a7f-17597c230987" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315419 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{8}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315419 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315419 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "33699acb-a73f-5709-9040-a47e293edf3f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315461 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315461 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315461 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3bc83917-1cfa-542d-8353-d1860b1c223e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315622 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315622 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315622 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "572ac41e-144e-58a4-9750-8a1cece44b7b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315730 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315730 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315730 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6c73414f-cf97-5567-81bf-1d9361692fcf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317005 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186315399 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317005 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186315419 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317005 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186315461 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317005 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186315622 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317005 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186315730 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317005 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317005 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317005 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186315461 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317005 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c1d73278-34a9-5b7e-8976-1f41a381eee7" #edb/ref 175