17] [17592186351507 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186351018 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351507 #edb/ref 1069 "q-83402" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351507 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351507 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨2t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡t⟩$ for $t>0$, use the cross product curvature formula to compute the curvature at the point $P(2,1,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351507 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "62f8ada8-0edf-581d-85ea-b6a85fd96890" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351507 #edb/ref 1074 "The curvature $κ(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to the point $P(2,1,0)$ on the given curve. We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨2,1,0⟩ \\\\ ⟨2t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡t⟩ & =⟨2,1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the respective components gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2t=2 \\\\ {t}^{2}=1 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡t=0.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equality, $t=1.$ This value also satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, $P(2,1,0)$ is at the tip of $r(1).$ \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$, ${r}^{′}(1),$  and $‖{r}^{′}(1)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,2t,\\,\\frac{1}{t}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(1) & =⟨2,2,1⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${r}^{″}(t)$ and ${r}^{″}(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(1) & =⟨0,2,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross-product and its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(1)\\times {r}^{″}(1) & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-4i+2j+4k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(1)\\times {r}^{″}(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+4+16} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature at $t=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(1) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(1)\\times {r}^{″}(1)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(1){‖}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{{3}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351624 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{3t}{4(1+{t}^{4})^{3/2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351624 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351624 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "06cbc6f5-dd74-546a-b75d-90d4feb0f218" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351763 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{2t}{3(1+{t}^{4})^{3/2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351763 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351763 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "167fbbff-610a-5ffc-98a4-f7a7c22e90c7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352251 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{(1+{t}^{4})^{3/2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352251 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352251 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4a7368fb-0ce5-5371-9c5e-757a189fdc4e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352589 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt{1+{t}^{4}}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352589 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352589 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "74a4ce6e-c86a-57cb-910b-11b5b57f298c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352859 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{1+{t}^{4}}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352859 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352859 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "94e029dc-a141-5cc4-b20b-d0417f2a0541" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353919 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186351624 #edb/ref 17592186045417]